4
00:00:26,020 --> 00:00:33,020
A Bioscience Way of Life, Lesson 4.4, Everyday Biotechnology

5
00:00:33,020 --> 00:00:39,020
You completed Lesson 4.3, Animal Applications, during which you performed ELISA tests,

6
00:00:39,020 --> 00:00:47,020
completed a marker-assisted selection simulation, and discussed disease diagnoses and genetic abnormalities.

7
00:00:47,020 --> 00:00:54,020
This presentation provides information about how biotechnology is used in other aspects of everyday life.

8
00:00:54,020 --> 00:00:58,020
First, consider everything you have done since waking up this morning.

9
00:00:58,020 --> 00:01:04,020
Pause the video and write a short list of activities you have taken part in so far today.

10
00:01:04,020 --> 00:01:11,020
Resume the video to reveal a short list of everyday products produced through biotechnology applications.

11
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:22,200
As you look at this list, do you see any items on your list? Have you eaten, worn, or been transported by a product of biotechnology?

12
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:28,950
Did you list any additional biotechnology applications?

13
00:01:28,950 --> 00:01:32,950
Dietary energy availability is shown in the map here.

14
00:01:32,950 --> 00:01:39,950
Across the globe, dietary energy, nutrient availability, and malnutrition are the greatest health problems.

15
00:01:39,950 --> 00:01:46,950
According to the World Food Program, improper nutrition is more prevalent than any single disease.

16
00:01:46,950 --> 00:01:52,950
Improper diet is caused by many factors, some more manageable than others.

17
00:01:52,950 --> 00:01:56,950
How can biotechnology contribute to the solution?

18
00:01:56,950 --> 00:01:59,950
Pause the video to consider this question.

19
00:01:59,950 --> 00:02:08,020
Record your thoughts in your notes. Resume the video when you are finished.

20
00:02:08,020 --> 00:02:16,020
Be ready to discuss the potential effects of current biotechnologies, as well as acceptance of GM foods with your classmates.

21
00:02:16,020 --> 00:02:26,720
Now think of additional methods of producing energy using biotechnology.

22
00:02:26,720 --> 00:02:37,040
Pause the video, record any ideas you have, and resume the video when you are finished.

23
00:02:37,040 --> 00:02:43,040
Bioremediation is a process that uses microorganisms to convert pollutants into safe byproducts.

24
00:02:43,040 --> 00:02:47,040
Where could bioremediation be of assistance?

25
00:02:47,040 --> 00:03:01,550
Biotechnology also has many uses in human health, from developing new, more targeted medicines to faster, better, and more reliable diagnostic tests.

26
00:03:01,550 --> 00:03:07,550
Organisms can even be engineered to produce medicines in a process called farming.

27
00:03:07,550 --> 00:03:15,030
One such product is insulin.

28
00:03:15,030 --> 00:03:21,030
More intriguing yet are the questions here. How will biotechnology change everyday life in the future?

29
00:03:21,030 --> 00:03:26,030
Pause the video as you consider these questions and record your thoughts.

30
